    "ls|LS16_S14_U_425": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE\n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.425\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 5.2.2018\n \n \n \nDOCUMENTATION OF MONUMENTS\n \n \n \n425.\n \n \nSHRI PARVESH SAHIB SINGH:\n \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of CULTURE  be pleased to state: \n \n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether the Archaeological\n \nSurvey of India (ASI) has documented the number \nof monuments and historical sites that are prone to submergence in the low \nlying areas of river banks in the country and if so, the details thereof; and\n \n \n(b)\n \nthe conservation measures carried out to protect\n \nthem when they emerge during \ndroughts and when they submerge during monsoon?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR CULTURE AND \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE\n \n \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA)\n \n(a)\n \nAs per the latest informat\nion collected from field offices of ASI out of 3686 \nmonuments / sites, fourteen monuments / sites are found to be prone to \nsubmergence/submerged. The list is at Annexure.\n \n \n(b)\n \nAt present, two monuments of ASI in Assam, namely, (i) the rock known as \nBiswan\nath Sivalinga, Biswanath and (ii) the carvings, inscriptions and pillar on \nthe Urbasi island, Kamarup, emerge when the river level of Brahmaputra \nrecedes.  The ASI carries out regular cleaning and conservation work of these \nmonuments when water level reced\ne.\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \nANNEXURE \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 425 FOR 5.2.2018\n \n(\ni\n)\n \nLIST OF CENTRALLY PROETCTED MONUMENTS / SITES FOUND TO BE \nPRONE TO SUBMERGENCE \n \nSl. No.\n \nName of Monument/Site\n \nState\n \n \n1\n \nAnanta Sayi Vishnu, S\naranga\n \nOdisha\n \n2\n \nKapilesvara Mahadeva Temple, Hatuary\n \n3\n \nSimhanatha Mahadeva Temple, Gopinathpur\n \n4\n \nJagannath Temple, Jajpur\n \n5\n \nVarahanatha Temple, Jajpur\n \n6\n \nAsurgarh Fort, Kalahandi\n \n7\n \nBhubaneswar Mahadev Temple, Balia\n \n \n(\nii\n)\n \nLIST OF CENTRALLY PROETCTED \nMONUMENTS / SITES SUBMERGED \nDUE TO CONSTRUCTION OF RESERVOIR/DAM\n \nSl. No.\n \nName of Monument/Site\n \nState\n \n \n1\n \nTemples in five villages (Villages: Tangeda, \nEliampeta, Ketavaram, Kolluru, \nRegulagadda)\n \nAndhra Padesh\n \n2\n \nRatta Inscription in Narayandeva temple \n \nKarn\nataka\n \n3\n \nOne Archaeological Site\n \n4\n \nAncient Site Venivadar, Amreli\n \nGujarat\n \n5\n \nRock carving of Devi riding on a lion\n \nJammu& Kashmir\n \n6\n \nRock carving of Sitala, Narada, Brahma\n \n7\n \nRadha Krishna, Visveshwara and other \ncaves temples \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S14_U_426": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 426 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 26.03.2018 \n \nSCHEMES FOR BEEDI WORKERS \n \n†*426. SHRI RAJU SHETTY: \n \nWill the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to \nstate:  \n \n(a)the total number of beedi workers in the country at present, \nState/UT-wise; \n(b)the details of the schemes being run by the Government for the \nwelfare of beedi workers; \n(c)the details of the allocation made and expenditure incurred under \nthese schemes during t he last three years and the current year, \nscheme and State/UT-wise; \n(d)whether any study has been conducted/proposed to be conducted to \n     assess the impact of the said schemes on the living standard of the \nbeedi workers; and \n(e)if so, the details and the findings thereof and if not, the reasons      \ntherefor? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (IC) FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI SANTOSH KUMAR GANGWAR) \n \n \n(a) to (e):  Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n****       ****** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (e) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 426 FOR 26.03.2018 BY SH. RAJU \nSHETTY REGARDING SCHEMES FOR BEEDI WORKERS. \n \na) the number of registered Beedi workers in the country is at \nAnnexure- A. \n \nb) the details of the schemes being run by the Government for the \nwelfare of beedi workers is at Annexure-B. \n \nc) the details of the allocation made and expenditure incurred \nunder these schemes during  the last three years and the current \nyear, scheme and State/UT-wise is at Annexure –C. \n \nd) & e) As per the directions of Ministry of Finance regarding \ncontinuation of ongoing Central Government  Schemes beyond \n12th  Five Year Plan, third party evaluation of the Labour Welfare \nSchemes has been conducted and the report has been submitted.  \n \n  \n\nANNEXURE-A \n \nState/UT-wise details of registered Beedi Workers \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \nSl.No. Name of  \nRegion \nName of \nState/UT \nTotal \n1.  Ahmedabad Gujarat 42008 \n2.  Ajmer Rajasthan 42813 \n3.  Allahabad Uttar Pradesh 450228 \n4.  Bangalore Karnataka 244412 \n5.  Bhubaneswar Odisha 157753 \n6.  Hyderabad Andhra Pradesh/ \nTelangana \n412984 \n7.  Jabalpur Madhya Pradesh 1054652 \n8.  \n \nKolkata West Bengal 1658401 \nTripura 13385 \n9.  Guwahati  9154 \n10.  Kannur Kerala 32032 \n11.  \n \nNagpur Maharashtra 188550 \nGoa - \nDaman (UT) - \nDadra & Nagar \nHaveli (UT) \n- \n12.  Patna Bihar 293916 \n13.  Raipur Chhattisgarh 18757 \n14.  Tirunelveli Tamil Nadu 79905                        \n15.  Ranchi Jharkhand 113408 \n Total  4812358 \n\nANNEXURE-B \n \n1. HEALTH SCHEMES: \n \nBesides providing health care facilities to these workers through 12 Hospitals and 286 \nDispensaries located across the country, the following assistance is given to workers for \ntreatment of  certain categories of diseases, as under :-  \n \n \n2. HOUSING SCHEME: \nRevised Integrated Housing Scheme (RIHS), 2016 for beedi workers is being \nimplemented in the country through Welfare Commissioners of the Labour Welfare Organisation  \nunder this Ministry. The housing subsidy of Rs. 1,50,000/ -  is disbursed in three installments in \nthe ratio of 25:60:15.  \n  \nS. \nNo. PURPOSE NATURE OF ASSITANCE \n     1 Tuberculosis \nReservation of beds in T.B. Hospitals and domiciliary \ntreatment for workers. Subsistence allowance of Rs. \n750/- to Rs. 1000/ - p.m. is granted as per the advice \nof the treating physician. \n2 Heart Diseases Reimbursement of expenditure up to Rs. 1,30,000/- to \nworkers. \n3 Kidney \nTransplantation \nReimbursement of expenditure up to Rs. 2,00,000/- to \nworkers. \n4 Cancer \nReimbursement of actual expenses on treatment, \nmedicines and diet charges incurred by workers, or \ntheir dependents. \n5 \nMinor surgery like \nHernia, \nAppendectomy, Ulcer \nGynecological \ndiseases and Prostrate \ndiseases. \nReimbursement of expenditure up to Rs. 30 ,000/- to \nworkers and their dependents. \n\n3. FINANCIAL ASSISTANCE FOR EDUCATION OF THE WARDS OF \nBEEDI WORKERS. \n \n \n  \nSCHEME Nature of assistance \nScheme for award \nof scholarships to \nthe wards  of beedi \nworkers \nScholarship is awarded to the children of the  \nworkers at the following rates per student per year:- \nGroup Class Rates \nGirls Boys \nGroup I Class  I to IV 250 250 \nGroup  II Class V to VIII 940 500 \nGroup III Class IX  1140 700 \nGroup \nIV \nClass X 1840 1400 \nGroup V Class XI to XII 2440 2000 \n ITI 10000 10000 \nGroup \nVI \nNon-Professional \nDegree Courses; Non -\nProfessional Post \nGraduate Courses; \nTwo-Three Year \nDiploma Courses and \nBCA,BBA and PGDCA. \n3000 3000 \nGROUP \nVII \nProfessional Degree \nCourses \ni.e.B.E./B.Tech/ MBBS/ \nBAMS/BUMS/ B.Sc . \n(Agriculture) and MCA/ \nMBA. \n15000 15000 \n \n\nANNEXURE-C \n \n  \nRegions \n  \n  \nEducation \n2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 \nBudget \nallocated\n(Rs. in \n,000) \nExpendit\nure (Rs. \nin ,000) \nBudget \nallocated\n(Rs. in \n,000) \nExpendit\nure (Rs. \nin ,000) \nBudget \nallocated \n(Rs. in \n,000) \nExpendit\nure (Rs. \nin ,000) \nBudget \nallocated \n(Rs. in \n,000) \nExpendi\nture   \n(Rs. in \n,000) \nH.Q 0 0 0 0 \n \n150812  814574  123601 \nAjmer  27530 20106  29390 4499  29390 10  1268  12 \nAllahabad  20235 4851  21219 1111  21219 6152  1111  57 \nBangalore  198450 166140  210050 98321  210050 128392  13459  40055 \nBhubaneswar  53550 45217  56730 20070  56730 166  2066  626 \nHyderabad  221550 168615  234198 285321  234198 261404  1358  16602 \nJabalpur  24600 21892  26077 19933  26077 3  2062  1853 \nKarma  12070 4495  14910 86  14910 65  1091  52 \nKolkata  212844 188252  226110 383373  241810 230765  11064  56 \nNagpur  55075 48563  56816 23119  41116 199  1057  300 \nTotal  825904 668131  875500 835833  875500 777968  849141  183214 \nRegions \n  \n  \nHealth \n2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 \nBudget \nal